Z||000000||Simple Fiero||08-07-2001||11:26 PM||||I am trying to figure out if I have a izuzu or a getrag. I have a stock 88 coupe 4 cyl. the reason behind this is, one of the guys up here that drives an 86 went to look at a master slave for his clutch and he came up with getrag at napa for his. That is why i am wondering, he has the 86 coupe 4 cyl. Both are 5 speeds. Don't flame me I am new to this mechanical stuff. And yes my 1 st gear is really really short.<BR>Also what is the power difference between mine and his. He seems to be longer geared than me.<BR>Thanks guys and gals||||reg||5
Z||000001||aubicon||08-08-2001||12:15 AM||||i had a trany question, yesterday and someone informed me the the getrag has a dipstick that screws into the trany and the end cap is steel (the endcap is located on the furthest end from the engine, rite by the drivers side rear wheel well) just reach in there with a magnet and see if it sticks, the rest of the trany is aluminum and the magnet will not stick to that so make sure that you get it on the very end of the trany. I hope that this will help.||||reg||1
Z||000002||StuGood||08-08-2001||08:13 AM||||The stock 4-cylinder manual transaxle Fieros all have 5-speed Isuzus... (except for the 1984 models, which I don't know about).  I would bet your next paycheck (after all, it's your money  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif">) that you have an Isuzu.<P>For me, the easiest way to identify an Isuzu trans. installed in a Fiero is:  The shifter cables in the engine compartment make a big rainbow arch over the top, on their way to the trans.  If there's any doubt, try the magnet test aubicon suggested.     ||||reg||1
Z||000003||88CoupeV6||08-08-2001||10:46 AM||||Here is how the shift cables go on an isuzu. On the getrag there is one up and one under.  <IMG SRC="http://albums.photopoint.com/j/View?u=1249362&a=9233482&p=30056813&Sequence=0&res=high"> <P>------------------<BR>Josh<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://people.ne.mediaone.net/fiero64/Fiero642.jpg">   <BR><B>Also 88 Yellow GT</B> :D  <BR><A HREF="http://albums.photopoint.com/j/AlbumList?u=1249362" TARGET=_blank>My pics</A>||||reg||7
Z||000004||Simple Fiero||08-08-2001||08:07 PM||||This just proves AGAIN! That we know more about our cars than most dealers and shops and parts stores. Thanks for your help guys, speacially the pic that was a huge help. I now know what I have, and can tell napa to shove it. LOL||||reg||6
